  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Health Recovery in North East Syria Project (HERNES 2)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&lt;p&gt;The approach is two-pronged. On the one hand, and to secure the achievements reached by HERNES 1, the project intends to continue to support the delivery of basic health services, as well as maternity care in the 7 facilities currently supported.On the other hand, EF intends to further contribute to lay the foundation for a more durable recovery of the health sector in the NES. This will be achieved through ensuring that the work that is performed in the supported centers can form the basis for a greater harmonization and coordination of practices, protocols and guidelines. To this purpose, EF will provide technical assistance to the Health Working Group under the NES in the fields of Reproductive Maternal Newborn and Child Health (RMNCH) and Supply Chain Management. EF also intends to support NES health actors policy dialogue on the recovery and future prospects of a stabilized and functioning health system in Syria and strengthen its support to capacity building through trainings of and support to health workers.&lt;/p&gt;</narrative>
  </description>
